{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>The daughter of my master's brother, for his son.</b> This is the plain sense: ותהדין (and this one) guided me to the family and relatives of my master. And the נקודה over which he mentions 'taken' (הלקוחים) is dotted with a chirik, singular form — meaning, to take the daughter of one of the relatives of my master."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The Hebrew appears textually difficult. קדמאה בציר״ה may mean 'the plain sense in short'; the letters ציר״ה possibly form an abbreviation. The phrase והדין likely connects to the following clause rather than standing alone. Transmitted hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:44.685839116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}